    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass (the suite has a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule following the codebase's existing conventions for per-day/count-derived owner attributes (mirroring `NamesakeCounter` and `DailyRegistrationLimiter`).\n\n**What the rule does:** on create, when more than 80 owners already carry the new owner's effective registration date, the owner's `bulkSignupWarning` is set to `true`; otherwise `false`. The value is captured as a snapshot at create time (like `namesakeCount`), so it's returned consistently on both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`BulkSignupWarningAssigner`** (new component) \u2014 single responsibility: counts already-stored owners sharing the new owner's registration date via the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersByRegistrationDate` and sets the flag when the count exceeds the threshold (80). Runs before save so it doesn't count itself.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`, `@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected the new assigner and invoked it in `addOwner` alongside the other pre-save assigners.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it (no mapper changes needed).\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column to the `owners` table.\n\nI reused the existing `countOwnersByRegistrationDate` service method and the established assigner pattern rather than duplicating counting logic or expanding the controller with inline logic.",
